From 7324299de36a7e409eb6c1067e83866a3b01db23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Matthias P. Walther" <matthiaspeterw@aol.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 23:21:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hwdb: map mic-mute key on Logitech K950 (Bluetooth)

The mic-mute key on the Logitech K950 keyboard (046D:B388, Bluetooth)
emits BTN_0 (scancode 0x100e1) instead of a usable key, so it does
nothing under GNOME/KDE. Map it to KEY_MICMUTE, its intended function.

Scancode determined with evtest on the device.

(cherry picked from commit 7961b4a78df9723e0de1fcac762f4d6e2d7b622b)

Related: RHEL-72703
---
 hwdb.d/60-keyboard.hwdb | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hwdb.d/60-keyboard.hwdb b/hwdb.d/60-keyboard.hwdb
index 0494f0311f..097714d8b8 100644
--- a/hwdb.d/60-keyboard.hwdb
+++ b/hwdb.d/60-keyboard.hwdb
@@ -1432,6 +1432,10 @@ evdev:input:b0005v046DpB317*
  KEYBOARD_KEY_70047=brightnessdown
  KEYBOARD_KEY_70048=brightnessup
 
+# Logitech K950
+evdev:input:b0005v046DpB388*
+ KEYBOARD_KEY_100e1=micmute                             # Mic-mute key emits BTN_0
+
 # iTouch
 evdev:input:b0003v046DpC308*
  KEYBOARD_KEY_90001=shop                                # Shopping
